    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "terrainName": "basic-desert",
    "description": "What: a napalm strike (CE-3487 flame FL-3, F-5; docs/designs/weapons/DESIGN_Flame_Weapons.md \u00a77b). On basic-desert an 'A-10 Napalm' (the A-10 with a Mk 77 firebomb rack) starts 4.1 km west at 300 m and is ordered AirPlatformStrike on the line of three unarmed hostiles at (600, 300) ('Line Man 1..3', within 6 m of it). The firebomb lays its fire in an 80 x 25 m ellipse along the flight line: the fireball sets every man inside alight, and the ground burns for 300 s. 'Late Man' (hostile, unarmed) starts 130 m north and walks south through the strike point at 1.5 m/s, reaching the burning ground long after the fireball - only the ground fire can burn him. 'Far Car' stands 50 m north of the axis. Judge: one firebomb released and bursting; the three line men set alight and dead; the Late Man hurt by the ground fire (never caught by the fireball); the Far Car untouched."
  },
